index 0000000..1fb4ad0
--- /dev/null
+++ b/src/graphics/shaders/xesl/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,17 @@
+# Resolve shader sources (16 and 32 bpp)
+
+From Xenia (BSD license, https://github.com/xenia-project/xenia) at commit 04d5c40d0d, which compiles to the same
+bytecode as the shipped `resolve_full_*` headers. Changed: `resolve.xesli` reads the destination number format
+(RB_COPY_DEST_INFO bits 13 to 15) and `resolve_full_16bpp.xesli` stores integers for the integer number formats
+instead of normalized values, and `resolve_full_32bpp.xesli` stores truncated integers (signed in two's complement)
+for them. Trials Fusion resolves its virtual texture page table as 16 bpp integers, and Trials Evolution its
+occlusion depth pyramid as signed 16_16.
+
+Compile from the `gpu` folder:
+
+    fxc /nologo /T cs_5_1 /O3 /D SHADING_LANGUAGE_HLSL_XE=1 /Vn resolve_full_16bpp_cs /Fh resolve_full_16bpp_cs.h resolve_full_16bpp.cs.xesl
+    fxc /nologo /T cs_5_1 /O3 /D SHADING_LANGUAGE_HLSL_XE=1 /Vn resolve_full_16bpp_scaled_cs /Fh resolve_full_16bpp_scaled_cs.h resolve_full_16bpp_scaled.cs.xesl
+    fxc /nologo /T cs_5_1 /O3 /D SHADING_LANGUAGE_HLSL_XE=1 /Vn resolve_full_32bpp_cs /Fh resolve_full_32bpp_cs.h resolve_full_32bpp.cs.xesl
+    fxc /nologo /T cs_5_1 /O3 /D SHADING_LANGUAGE_HLSL_XE=1 /Vn resolve_full_32bpp_scaled_cs /Fh resolve_full_32bpp_scaled_cs.h resolve_full_32bpp_scaled.cs.xesl
+
+and copy the headers to `../bytecode/d3d12_5_1`.
